export const privacyMarkdown =
  '_Last updated: August 5, 2026_\n\nCareer Source Group, LLC ("Career Source Group," "we," "us") respects your privacy. This policy\nexplains what information we collect through this website, how we use it, and who we share it with.\n\n## Information we collect\n\nWe collect information you provide directly, through one of three forms:\n\n- **Contact form** — name, email, phone, and the message you send us.\n- **Request Talent** (client intake) — name, email, phone, company name, the specialty and\nengagement type you\'re hiring for, and any additional details you provide.\n- **Find Opportunities** (candidate application) — name, email, phone, location, specialty, and\navailability, plus a résumé and, if you choose to include them, a portfolio URL and LinkedIn URL.\n\nWe also automatically collect standard technical information when you visit — your IP address and\nbasic request metadata — used only to secure the site (rate-limiting abusive form submissions) and\nto operate it. We do not currently run any analytics or advertising tracking; see "Cookies" below.\n\n## How we use your information\n\nWe use the information you submit to:\n\n- Respond to your inquiry, requirement, or application;\n- Match candidates to roles and clients to talent;\n- Protect the site and our forms against spam and abuse; and\n- Meet our legal and accounting obligations.\n\nWe do not sell your personal information, and we do not use it for behavioral advertising.\n\n## Where your information is stored and who we share it with\n\nYour submissions are stored in our database, hosted by Supabase. A résumé you upload is kept in\nprivate file storage that only our staff can access, through short-lived signed links — it is never\nmade public. We use the following service providers to operate the site and process submissions;\neach acts on our behalf and does not use your information for its own purposes:\n\n- **Supabase** — database and file storage for form submissions and résumés.\n- **Resend** — delivers the email notifications and confirmations our forms send.\n- **Cloudflare Turnstile** — a bot-check that runs when you submit a form, to keep spam out.\n\nOne embedded service is not under our control and sets its own cookies:\n\n- **Calendly** — if you click a scheduling link, Calendly\'s own booking widget opens and\nCalendly, not us, sets cookies to run that scheduler. See\n[Calendly\'s privacy policy](https://calendly.com/privacy).\n\n## Cookies\n\nThis site does not run advertising or analytics cookies. The only cookies set on this site are the\nones described above under Calendly — from a third-party widget we embed, whose data collection we\ndo not control. Your theme preference (light or dark) is saved in your browser\'s local storage, not\na cookie, and never leaves your device.\n\n## Data retention\n\nWe keep the information you submit for as long as reasonably necessary to respond to your inquiry,\nconsider your application, or maintain business records, and no longer than that. You can ask us to\ndelete your information at any time — see "Your rights" below.\n\n## Your rights\n\nYou can ask what personal information we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete\nit, by contacting us through our [Contact page](/contact). We will respond to reasonable requests.\n\n## International visitors\n\nWe are based in the United States, and information you submit is stored and processed in the United\nStates. If you are contacting or applying to us from outside the United States, your information\nwill be transferred to and processed in the United States.\n\n## Children\'s privacy\n\nThis site is not directed at, and we do not knowingly collect information from, anyone under the age\nof 18.\n\n## Changes to this policy\n\nWe may update this policy from time to time to reflect changes to the site or our practices. The\ndate above shows when it was last revised.\n\n## Contact us\n\nQuestions about this policy or your information can be sent through our\n[Contact page](/contact), or by mail to the address listed in our [Legal Notice](/legal-notice).';

