  '_Last updated: August 5, 2026_\n\nThis notice explains how Career Source Group, LLC ("Career Source Group," "we," "us") handles the\ninformation you provide when you apply through our Find Opportunities form. It supplements our\ngeneral [Privacy Policy](/privacy), which covers the rest of this website.\n\n## What we collect\n\nWhen you apply, we collect your name, email, phone, location, specialty, and availability, plus a\nrésumé and, if you choose to include them, a portfolio URL and LinkedIn URL. Depending on the role\nand region, we may also ask for your work authorization status and compensation expectations\n(hourly rate, annual salary, or monthly rate).\n\n## How we use it\n\nWe use this information only to match you with relevant opportunities across our client network.\n**We do not submit your profile to a client without discussing the opportunity with you first and\nreceiving your permission.** Joining our talent network does not guarantee placement.\n\n## How your résumé and sensitive details are handled\n\nYour résumé is stored in private file storage that only our staff can access, through short-lived\nsigned links generated at the time of viewing — it is never made public or searchable. Your résumé\nupload, compensation figures, and work-authorization details are transmitted only over HTTPS and\nare never logged in our analytics.\n\n## Retention\n\nWe keep your profile for as long as reasonably necessary to consider you for relevant\nopportunities, or until you ask us to delete it. See "Your rights" below.\n\n## Your rights\n\nYou can ask what information we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete it at\nany time, by contacting us through our [Contact page](/contact). We will respond to reasonable\nrequests.\n\n## Questions\n\nQuestions about this notice can be sent through our [Contact page](/contact). For how we handle\ndata collected elsewhere on this site, see our full [Privacy Policy](/privacy).';
